# Star Fox 64 (US 1.1), as patched by Auztin's Archipelago world. Addresses come from the
# inspectredc/sf64 decomp: its main segment is ROM 0x1050 at 0x80000450 and is loaded by the
# boot code as it is, so vram = rom + 0x7FFFF400 there. The world's patch changes only 0x64
# bytes of it (ROM 0x59A8, its loader); its hooks into the game are written at run time
# (src/inject.c), and none of them is near anything used here.
#
# STUB_VRAM is __rmonGetThreadStatus, in libultra's remote debugger (rmon), which only runs
# under Nintendo's development tools. Nothing in the ROM refers to rmonMain or osInitRdb,
# the only ways in, so the debugger thread is never created and its functions are called
# only by each other. Measured too, with the world's own connector live: 0 calls at its
# entry, +0x100 and +0x200, at rmonMain and at __rmonExecute over 29,040 frames of play,
# while Lib_DmaRead ran 35 times, and none of its 756 bytes ever changed.
STUB_VRAM=0x8002BE38
STUB_MAX=756

# The Expansion Pak, above the 2 MB the world reserves for itself (0x80400000..0x80600000,
# `.area 0x00200000` in its build.asm). Over that session only 14 of the Pak's 1024 pages
# were touched, all at 0x80400000..0x8040E000: the world's own payload. ram-bounds.py over
# the main segment and the payload finds nothing bracketing 0x80700000.
AGENT_VRAM=0x80700000

# Past the end of the world's ROM, which is always 0xC0DD70 bytes: one patched ROM serves
# every seed (the world asserts its md5), with the payload appended at 0xC00000.
AGENT_ROM=0xC10000
AGENT_MIN_RAM=0x800000
